cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its lab lists, please cite it as below, and cite the original data sources listed in docs/data_sources.md."
title: "amine-co2-uq: uncertainty-aware screening of amine mixtures for CO2 capture"
abstract: >-
  A calibrated aqueous-amine equilibrium model, with Monte Carlo and conformal uncertainty,
  screens about 23,000 amine mixtures at 30 wt% total amine for cement and coal flue gas.
  A practical stage converts regeneration energy, solvent make-up, corrosion and viscosity
  into one running cost in USD per tonne of CO2, and produces ranked lists of mixtures for
  laboratory testing.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Saha
    given-names: Mayukh
    affiliation: "Birla Institute of Technology and Science (BITS)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-06
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/frozenexplorer/uq-amine"
keywords:
  - carbon capture
  - CO2 absorption
  - amine blends
  - piperazine
  - vapour-liquid equilibrium
  - uncertainty quantification
  - conformal prediction
